# Build context for docker/Dockerfile. Everything `npm run build:headless`
# needs stays in; host-platform build output and native modules stay out —
# node_modules especially, since the host's is compiled for darwin and the
# image rebuilds node-pty against the container's Node ABI.
#
# docker/entrypoint.sh is deliberately NOT excluded — it ships in the image.
# So is resources/: it holds permission-prompt-mcp.js and mcp-bridge.js,
# without which Chat-tab approvals and ness-control tools silently vanish.
docker/compose.yaml
docker/compose.host-claude.yaml
node_modules
out
dist
dist-headless
release
.headless-data
.git
.github
site
plans
release-notes
build
*.log
.env
.DS_Store
